<problem>
<!-- <title>Half life </title> -->

<setup>

<selectFromSequence name="a" from=".3" to=" .9" step=" .1" />
<selectFromSequence name="b" from="3" to=" 60" step=" 7" />
<select name="n">n t </select>
<select name="x">alpha  beta  gamma  delta  epsilon  mu  nu  tau  sigma  omega  zeta </select>
<math name="ans" simplify="full">log(.5)/log($a )</math>
<math name="A" simplify="full">$a -1</math>

</setup>


<p>Find the half-life for the system below
<md>
<mrow>$x _{$n+1} \amp= $a $x _$n </mrow>
<mrow>$x _0 \amp = $b </mrow>
</md>

</p>
<p>
The half-life is 
<answer name="answer1">
<award allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001">$ans </award>
<award credit="0.5" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$ans </award>
<award credit="0.25" allowedErrorInNumbers="0.1" feedbackCodes="numericalerror">$ans </award>
</answer>
$answer1.feedbacks

</p>
<p>

(Keep at least four significant digits in your response.)
</p>



<solution>
<p>The dynamical system is in function iteration form.  We can immediately calculate the half life.</p>
<p>
The half life is <m>\frac{  \log \frac{1}{2} }{ \log $a  } = <round numDigits="4"><number>$ans </number></round></m>
</p>

</solution>


</problem>